# Everything in this repo is built and run inside Linux containers or WSL, so LF is the
# only correct line ending in a working copy -- not just in the stored blob.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows checks these out as CRLF, and a shell script with CRLF
# fails inside a container with an error that names a line number rather than the cause:
#   ./e2e.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
# The same applies to the Dockerfiles' RUN lines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.gz  binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
